From f49f424d1bf63d636b4f823fea757a3f0ed455c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:57:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] storage: add write_file for Lua and Python scripts

Lua scripts could read files (solaros.storage.read_file) but had no way
to write one, so Lua apps could not save state. Add
solaros.storage.write_file(path, data[, append]) to the shared script API,
for both Lua and Python:

- solar_os_storage_write_file() writes up to 64 KiB. Without append it
  writes and syncs "<path>.tmp", then swaps it in with the existing
  solar_os_storage_replace_file(), so a failed write never leaves a
  truncated file. With append it adds to the end (creating the file).
- Lua takes a binary-safe string, Python bytes or str; both raise the
  usual storage errors.
- Host test covers create/replace/append/binary/empty/too-big/bad args/
  directory/missing parent; manual pages document it; the script API
  count in test_script_binding_descriptor goes from 766 to 767.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B2S3WcfsAgHLdif2Kpvj91
